  "starterCode": "# Rotary Positional Embeddings — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(x, positions, theta=10000.0):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Rotary Positional Embeddings** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(x, positions, theta=10000.0):\n    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n    positions = np.asarray(positions, dtype=float)\n    dim = x.shape[-1]\n    if dim % 2: raise ValueError(\"last dimension must be even\")\n    inv = 1.0 / (theta ** (np.arange(0, dim, 2, dtype=float) / dim))\n    ang = positions[..., None] * inv\n    c, s = np.cos(ang), np.sin(ang)\n    even, odd = x[..., 0::2], x[..., 1::2]\n    out = np.empty_like(x)\n    out[..., 0::2] = even*c - odd*s\n    out[..., 1::2] = even*s + odd*c\n    return out.tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
